From: Hari Naraayana Desikan Kannan <quic_hnaraaya@quicinc.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:19:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AP: fix legacy station roaming between MLD links

When a station first attempts an MLO association and then reconnects as a
legacy station on another link, stale station state may remain on the
first link. Since all links of an AP MLD share one netdev, pruning that
stale entry also removes the active kernel station entry. This results
in repeated association and pruning until the stale entry expires.

Clear unauthorized MLD station state on partner links before re-adding a
station. When pruning a legacy station from another link of the same AP
MLD, free only the stale hostapd entry and preserve the shared kernel
entry.

Adapted to hostapd 2026.08.07. This also includes the later QSDK
follow-ups that immediately free the stale userspace entry instead of
retaining it until the inactivity timer expires, and recognize it even
after authorization has already been cleared.

Retain upstream link-address-change authentication and SA Query rollback.
The new ap_sta_reset_prev_assoc() helper disables the authorization check
when removing the earlier association, alongside FT and BSS teardown.
Do not restore the obsolete eager handle_assoc() reset path.

Signed-off-by: Hari Naraayana Desikan Kannan <quic_hnaraaya@quicinc.com>
Signed-off-by: Arunpandi Kannan <quic_arunpand@quicinc.com>
Co-developed-by: Manish Dharanenthiran <mdharane@qti.qualcomm.com>
